    {
      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 15: independently estimating CdA, C_rr, mass and wind — what the data can and cannot give",
      "text": "All four parameters are recoverable within the pre-stated plausible ranges for all three riders: mass from braking-free sustained climbs is CdA-robust (JAAM's implied 103 kg was genuine — rider-confirmed ≈ 100 ± 7 kg, retiring Entry 14's CdA-misspecification guess); CdA and C_rr become identifiable only once per-activity wind is modelled via a LINEARISED aero regression (flat-power, coast-down and climb-only methods all fail for CdA); the wind vector itself comes from GPS-bearing directional asymmetry, de-biased for regression attenuation.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
